# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repo is publishable. That is only true because of this file, so read it
# before adding anything.
#
# The rule: the repo may contain code, schema and documentation. It may not
# contain what is owned, what it cost, what it is worth, or any credential.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Credentials. NOTION_TOKEN, COCKPIT_PASSWORD, and anything added later.
# `.env.*` is here because `*.env` does NOT match `.env.local` - it matches
# files that END in .env. `vercel env pull` writes .env.local by default, so
# that gap was one command away from committing the deployment password.
.env
*.env
.env.*
!*.example.env

# The holdings list. portfolio.local.json is the single file that knows what is
# owned; portfolio.example.json is the committed schema and stays.
portfolio.local.json
*.local.json

# Working notes. CHECKPOINT.local.md quotes position sizes and the coverage
# measurement, so it stays local for the same reason the CSVs do. Anything
# named *.local.* is private by convention here.
*.local.md

# Broker exports - units, cost basis, account numbers, every transaction.
nordnet-ostoerittain*.csv
*.csv

# Generated: the dashboard embeds the entire book, and portfolio.json is it in
# plain text. Never commit out/.
out/

# Caches and run history. state/equity-log.json is the Notion board mirrored to
# disk - theses and targets - and history.jsonl is the book day by day.
state/

# The copy of the dashboard that gets uploaded to Vercel. Byte-identical to
# out/dashboard.html, so it is the book, so it is ignored for the same reason.
# deploy/ itself stays: middleware.ts, vercel.json and package.json are code and
# hold no credential - the password is an environment variable on Vercel.
deploy/public/
deploy/.vercel/
deploy/node_modules/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
